RAUC OTA signing keys

Files
  signing.key.pem: Private key for signing system and bootloader RAUC bundles.
  signing.cert.pem: Matching X.509 certificate installed on devices to verify bundles.
  These keys are independent of the secure boot keys, SSH CA and system.key.

Generate a key pair
  Run these commands in a new, empty directory. Do not overwrite an existing key.

  umask 077
  openssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:3072 -nodes -sha256 \
    -keyout signing.key.pem -out signing.cert.pem -days 3650 \
    -subj '/CN=NAOS Development OTA signing/' \
    -addext 'basicConstraints=critical,CA:TRUE' \
    -addext 'keyUsage=critical,digitalSignature,keyCertSign,cRLSign'
  chmod 600 signing.key.pem

Verify the certificate
  openssl verify -CAfile signing.cert.pem signing.cert.pem
  openssl x509 -in signing.cert.pem -noout -subject -dates -fingerprint -sha256

Devices must trust the certificate matching the signing key. Changing only the
build-side private key causes existing devices to reject the new bundles.
